course: dictionary
lesson: 3829
title: Formic acid and the ant sting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Formic is a word about ants. It is an adjective, so it describes a thing, and in science it is most often used in the phrase «formic acid». Formic comes from the Latin word for ant, formica.
explain: «Ants and nettles inject formic acid and other chemicals that irritate the nerves in your skin.» The sentence tells you what the acid does: it irritates your nerves. That is why an ant bite or a nettle sting feels itchy and burning.
explain: Acids and alkalis are opposites. Because formic acid is an acid, some people rub a mild alkali, such as soap, on a sting to ease it. A dock leaf is an old folk remedy for nettle stings, though it is not a scientific cure.
fact: Formic means to do with ants.
fact: «Formic acid» is a stinging acid made by ants and stinging nettles.
fact: Formic acid causes the itchy, burning feeling of an ant bite or nettle sting.
fact: Some birds sit on ant nests so the ants spray formic acid onto their feathers. This is called anting, and it helps clean the feathers.
fact: An acid is a substance that can irritate or sting, and an alkali, such as soap, can help to balance it.
exercise: «Ants and nettles inject formic acid and other chemicals that irritate the nerves in your skin.» What is formic acid? | A type of pollen | A soap that cleans your skin | *A stinging acid that causes itchy, burning skin | A sweet sugar found in flowers
exercise: Which of these words is to do with ants? | Nettle | Alkali | *Formic | Acid
exercise: Some people rub mild soap on a nettle sting. Why might this help? | Soap adds more formic acid to the sting | Soap is a strong acid that burns the sting away | *Soap is a mild alkali, which can ease the effect of an acid | Soap makes the nettle grow faster
test: Birds that sit on ant nests get their feathers cleaned by what? | Sugar from the nest | *Formic acid sprayed by the ants | Dock leaves | Soap and water
test: Which feeling does formic acid cause in your skin? | A cool, numb feeling | A glowing light | A sweet taste | *An itchy, burning feeling
exam: Which is the best description of formic acid? | *A stinging acid made by ants and stinging nettles | A harmless sugar from flowers | A metal found in rocks | A kind of alkali used in soap
